The fear check is only made when the monster is very close to you and
in line of sight.  6 times out of 7, it only makes them flee for 1d10
turns.  Monsters that are not adjacent to you will still cast haste
self, cure self, invisibility, aggravate monster, summon nasties, and
double trouble.  Some monsters that can be summoned by summon nasties
are unconcerned by the name of the Queen of the Valar.  (Specifically,
elf-lords, Elvenkings, and minotaurs.)

You are correct that they will not cast direct attack spells if they
can't attack you in hand-to-hand combat, however, so while on Elbereth
you will not be subjected to wizardly attack spells except those cast by
Thoth Amon (human), the Wizard of Yendor (human), the Dark One (human),
ki-rin (lawful minion), Archons (lawful minion), Neferet the Green
(human), guides (human), and apprentices (human).

So yes, Her name will protect you from being cursed by liches.
